{
  "alakazamMeasures": true,
  "version": 1,
  "description": {
    "morphology": "Posterior negativity over occipito-temporal cortex, pooled here over PO7 and PO8, isolated as the deviant-minus-control difference wave. Two windows are given because an early and a late vMMN are routinely distinguished; which one carries the effect depends on the deviated feature, so treat both as candidates and pre-specify the one you will report. Unlike the auditory MMN there is no diagnostic polarity inversion at the mastoids.",
    "meaning": "A pre-attentive index of visual regularity violation, usually read as a prediction-error signal from automatic sensory memory. It does not require attention to the deviant dimension, and it is the attention-independence that distinguishes it from the N2b and P3b that an actively discriminated oddball elicits.",
    "task": "Passive visual oddball, where the deviance is IRRELEVANT to the task the participant is performing (a demanding central task while the deviants appear peripherally, for instance). In a task where the deviant is the target, this window measures N2b and P3b instead, whatever it is labelled. The control condition should be an equiprobable or cross-block one, so the same physical stimulus is compared with itself: a plain deviant-minus-standard difference confounds mismatch with adaptation and with the physical stimulus difference."
  },
  "rows": [
    {
      "label": "vMMN_early",
      "start": 100,
      "stop": 200,
      "measure": "Mean Amplitude",
      "polarity": "Negative",
      "width": 100,
      "localPoints": 0,
      "fraction": 0.5,
      "refChannel": "",
      "channels": "{PO7 PO8}"
    },
